<title>DENMARK: Danish June yr/yr CPI up 2.2 pct (EU method).</title>
<headline>Danish June yr/yr CPI up 2.2 pct (EU method).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish consumer prices were 0.3 percent higher in June 1997 from May 1997 and 2.2 percent up on June 1996, as calculated by the EU method, the National Statistics Office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Under the traditional Danish national formula the respective figures would have been a 0.2 percent month-on-month rise and 2.4 percent up year-on-year.</p>
<p>    EU FORMULA		 June 1997   May 1997    June 1996</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)    +0.3	 +0.6	   -0.1</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)     +2.2	 +1.9	   +2.2</p>
<p>    Index (base 1994)	  102.3	102.0	  104.7</p>
<p>NATIONAL FORMULA</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)    +0.2	 +0.7	   -0.1</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)     +2.4	 +2.1	   +2.0</p>
<p>    Index (base 1980)	  204.6	204.1	  199.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' average expectations were for a 2.1 percent yr/yr rise from June 1996 according to the national formula.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
